    "caveats": [
      "`raw_payments.amount` is stored in cents; divide by 100.0 to report dollars.",
      "Payment totals represent recorded payment transactions, not necessarily finalized net revenue; payment methods can include coupons and gift cards, and zero-value payments are possible.",
      "There can be multiple payment records per order. Joining orders to payments duplicates order-level rows, so use `COUNT(DISTINCT raw_orders.id)` for order counts after that join.",
      "Joining customers to orders also repeats customer rows for customers with multiple orders; use distinct customer IDs when counting customers after joins.",
      "Orders span 2018-01-01 through 2018-04-09 only, so time-based results are limited to this period.",
      "`raw_orders.user_id` ranges only through 99 although there are 100 customers, so at least one customer may have no order; use a left join from customers when analyzing customers without orders.",
      "Order status is the current fulfillment or return status and is not a payment-status field. An order with a payment record is not necessarily equivalent to an order in a particular fulfillment status.",
      "An order may have no payment record, so inner joining orders to payments excludes unpaid or unrecorded-payment orders."
    ],
    "example_questions": [
      "What was total payment revenue by payment method in dollars?",
      "How many orders were placed each day, broken down by order status?",
      "Which customers placed the most orders?",
      "What percentage of customers placed at least one order?",
      "How many orders have multiple payment transactions, and what is their total payment amount?"
    ]
